        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add Zalo provider server",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add a provider-native Zalo Bot API server with token-in-path authentication and documented response/error shapes\n- support `getMe`, single-update `getUpdates`, `sendMessage`, `sendPhoto`, `sendChatAction`, and webhook lifecycle methods over GET or POST\n- deliver authenticated admin ingress through the normal polling queue or native top-level webhook event transport\n- redact bot and webhook credentials from recorder events\n- add CLI, manifest, package exports, docs, protocol tests, and the isolated OpenClaw bridge\n\nThe provider server contains no OpenClaw-specific behavior. OpenClaw config, env, target, and recorder translation remain under `src/openclaw/bridges/zalo.ts`.\n\nDepends on openclaw/openclaw#98768 for the primitive `ZALO_API_URL` seam and corrections to the existing Zalo bot identity/timestamp assumptions.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm verify` (38 files, 180 tests, coverage)\n- focused Zalo server, bridge, CLI, and production-package tests (33 tests)\n- actual compatibility roundtrip using OpenClaw's real Zalo `getMe`, `getUpdates`, and `sendMessage` functions against this server\n- current Zalo Bot Platform documentation checked for API paths, GET/POST support, native webhook payload, secret header, error envelope, bot identity fields, and epoch-millisecond dates\n- autoreview findings fixed: webhook secret recorder leak and wrapped webhook payload\n- timestamp and getMe findings were traced to stale OpenClaw assumptions and fixed in openclaw/openclaw#98768\n- final autoreview clean with no accepted/actionable findings\n",
